CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> The Constituent Assembly took about 2 years, 11 months and 18 days to draft the Constitution, with Dr B.R. Ambedkar as head of the Drafting Committee. The Constitution was adopted on 26 November 1949 and came into force on 26 January 1950. The Aikyamatya Sukta speaks of 'one counsel, one assembly, one mind'. "
   "(i) When did the Constitution come into force? (ii) Who headed the Drafting Committee? (iii) What is the minimum age to vote under universal adult franchise? (iv) How does the idea of the Aikyamatya Sukta relate to decision-making in a democracy?",
   "(i) 26 January 1950 (1). (ii) Dr B.R. Ambedkar (1). (iii) 18 years (1). (iv) It stresses decisions taken after consultation and consensus, which is the basis of democratic decision-making (2).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A citizen finds that an official order denies her a basic right. Article 14 guarantees equality before law and Article 21 protects life and personal liberty, so she decides to approach the Supreme Court under Article 32. A group of lawyers also files a Public Interest Litigation (PIL) for people who cannot approach the court themselves. "
   "(i) Which Article protects life and personal liberty? (ii) Which Article allows a citizen to go to the Supreme Court for rights? (iii) Give the full form of PIL. (iv) If the Supreme Court declares a law passed by Parliament invalid, what is this power called and why is it important?",
   "(i) Article 21 (1). (ii) Article 32 (1). (iii) Public Interest Litigation (1). (iv) Judicial review (1); it keeps laws within the Constitution and protects citizens' rights (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> In a tribal village, the Gram Sabha meets regularly and women take part in large numbers because one-third of seats in panchayats are reserved for them. The PESA Act, 1996 empowers Gram Sabhas in tribal areas. In a different country, a leader says, 'Elections once, and no questions later,' and bans opposition. "
   "(i) What is a Gram Sabha? (ii) Which Act empowers Gram Sabhas in tribal areas? (iii) Why is reservation for women in panchayats useful? (iv) Why is the leader's rule not truly democratic?",
   "(i) A village-level assembly of all adult voters (1). (ii) The PESA Act, 1996 (1). (iii) It increases the participation of women in local decision-making (1). (iv) Regular elections alone do not make a democracy: it also needs accountability, a free opposition and freedom of expression, which are missing here (2).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

